[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3942138807","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116585#issuecomment-3942138807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116585","id":3942138807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q-EO3","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T01:52:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T01:52:30Z","body":"The reason I expose these methods is to reduce some of the uncertainty around `Control` and `Container` nodes. For beginners, when they run into issues related to a control’s position or size, they end up wasting a lot of time just to form a vague idea: that `Control`s might need some time to update. For experienced developers, when they face the same problem, they’ll think, “Maybe I should use call_deferred—let me try that,” then either “Oh, call_deferred fixed it,” or “Still not working… Maybe I should wait a full second.”\r\n\r\nMy point is, we’ve all been in this situation so often that `call_deferred` has become a “silver bullet” for these issues. But when it doesn’t work, people start doubting their own ability or even questioning Godot’s stability. Either outcome undermines users’ confidence in building robust games with Godot.\r\n\r\nThat’s why I believe it’s necessary to help users understand why they previously had to use `call_deferred`, and introduce a new approach so they no longer have to rely on it everywhere. They’ll be able to write code based on understanding, not guesswork or trial and error.\r\n\r\nThat’s all I was thinking when I tried to implement this \"layout pending\" mechanism. But you’re right—I still can’t tell whether this is just a workaround or a complete, proper solution. Maybe there are better ways to reduce uncertainty around `Control` and `Container`, for example, does not use `call_deferred` to do children sorting in `Container`, I don't know the feasibility though.\r\n\r\nIf we just focused on fixing this history navigation issue, I can keep these methods internal.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3942138807/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944190963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116585#issuecomment-3944190963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116585","id":3944190963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rF5Pz","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/user